 - 2026-10-29 (31): Ghast and fireball, first patch: AI and projectile logic (`missing.md` entry 2; the model, skins and sounds are the second patch). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run (no `rustc` in the sandbox). `Kind::Ghast` (4 x 4 x 4, 10 health, drops 0..2 gunpowder, `hostile`, so Peaceful removes it); `Mob::ai_ghast` is `EntityGhast.updatePlayerActionState` (waypoint within 16 blocks, new one when reached or 60 away, a 0.1 push every 2..6 ticks if `isCourseTraversable`, the Java's use of the OLD distance kept; player within 64 and in sight: face them, `attackCounter` to 20, then `Ev::Fire` 4 blocks along its heading, counter -40; out of sight it runs back down); `Mob::step`: no gravity (`step_box`'s pull is put back), 0.91 drag a tick, `body_yaw = yaw`. `Fireball` (`EntityFireball`): 1 x 1 x 1, starts at rest, `acc` 0.1 along the aim (+ Gaussian 0.4 a component) with 0.95 drag (0.8 in water), the segment of each tick is searched for a block and for the player or a mob (boxes grown 0.3; any ghast is passed for 25 ticks, ponytail: the Java names the owner), bursts as `Ev::Burst` at the place it was at the start of the tick; the mob it hits takes `damage(0)`. `lib.rs`: `Ev::Burst` is `explode(p, 1.0, true)`; `explode` got `flame` (`Explosion.isFlaming`: in each destroyed cell now air over an opaque block, fire 1 time in 3, in reverse order); a tap on a fireball under the crosshair (nearer than the block, mob, boat or cart) calls `Mobs::deflect` (motion = look, `acc` = look x 0.1; no damage, no wear). Nether spawns: ghast 10 / pig zombie 10 (`BiomeGenHell`), `CAP_GHAST` = 2 of its own so a crowd of pigmen does not keep it out, `can_spawn` 1 try in 20 with a free 5 x 5 x 5 cell room and no ground, one a spawn. Not here: model, `ghast.png` / `ghast_fire.png` (`render/items.rs` draws a ghast as nothing and the fireball not at all), sounds (`cry` is silent for it; the charge and fireball sounds are not queued), the fireball's smoke, the dataWatcher skin flag (`Mob::charge > 10` is it), water / lava drag of the ghast, the knockback of the explosion on mobs. Tests: `mobs::tests::{a_ghast_charges_twenty_ticks_then_fires_and_never_falls, a_fireball_accelerates_bursts_on_what_it_meets_and_turns_when_punched}`, `the_nether_spawns_pig_zombies_only` is now `..._and_ghasts_only`; the fireball's numbers (burst at y 10.9 on the grass from 20 blocks up, 1.3 blocks short of the player, top speed 1.9) were checked in a Python model of the same steps. UNVERIFIED: that it compiles (`ai_ghast` / `Fireball::tick` use `physics::aabb_hits_solid`, `ray_box`, `JavaRandom::next_gaussian` as their signatures read), the `lib.rs` wiring, the feel of the ghast's drift and the spawn rate by eye. Run `cargo test --lib mobs` first.
